\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. All ye that pass by,
\par To Jesus draw nigh:
\par To you is it nothing that Jesus
\par should die?
\par Your ransom and peace,
\par Your surety He is:
\par Come, see if there ever was sorrow
\par like His.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He dies to atone
\par For sins not His own;
\par Your debt He hath paid, and your
\par work He hath done.
\par Ye all may receive
\par The peace He did leave,
\par Who made intercession:
\par My Father, forgive!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For you and for me
\par He prayed on the tree:
\par The prayer is accepted, the sinner
\par is free.
\par That sinner am I,
\par Who on Jesus rely,
\par And come for the pardon 
\par God cannot deny.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My pardon I claim;
\par For a sinner I am,
\par A sinner believing in Jesus's name.
\par He purchased the grace
\par Which now I embrace:
\par O Father, Thou know'st He hath
\par died in my place.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

